WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.050
Do you sometimes get angry?
你有时会生气吗？

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.380
Perhaps your answer is yes.
也许你的回答是肯定的。

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.730
Actually, everyone feels angry sometimes.
其实，每个人有时都会生气。

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.890
It’s part of being human.
这是人性的一部分。

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.630
However, anger is a strong feeling and it is not easy to control.
然而，愤怒是一种强烈的情绪，不容易控制。

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:21.560
Sometimes anger can be good, because it can encourage us to change things that make us unhappy.
有时候，愤怒可能是好事，因为它能促使我们去改变那些让自己不开心的事情。

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:29.280
“Anger is a normal feeling and it’s OK to have these feelings sometimes,” says Dr Nathwani, a psychologist.
心理学家纳特瓦尼博士说：“愤怒是一种正常的情绪，有时产生这样的情绪也没关系。”

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.260
It’s common for teenagers to feel angry.
青少年感到生气是很常见的。

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.340
First, the body’s hormones are changing, which can make feelings much stronger.
首先，身体里的激素正在变化，这可能会让情绪变得强烈得多。

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:44.350
Second, the part of the brain that helps to manage feelings doesn’t fully develop until you’re in your mid-20s.
其次，大脑中帮助管理情绪的那部分，要到二十五岁左右才会发育完全。

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.740
Being angry does not mean you are a grumpy person.
生气并不意味着你是个脾气坏的人。

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.330
Sometimes it suggests something else.
有时候，生气表明的是别的情况。

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:55.900
“Anger usually comes when we feel hurt, scared or unhappy,” says Dr Nathwani.
纳特瓦尼博士说：“愤怒通常在我们感到受伤害、害怕或不开心的时候出现。”

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.670
“It can be a strong feeling that we notice in our bodies.
“它可能是一种我们能在身体上察觉到的强烈情绪。

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.940
We may feel hot or our hearts may beat fast.”
我们可能会觉得身上发热，或者心跳得很快。”

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.800
Sometimes you might not even know why you’re feeling this way.
有时你甚至可能不知道自己为什么会有这种感觉。

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.280
Your anger is not always caused by your own stress or other people being unkind.
你的愤怒并不总是由自身的压力或别人的不友善引起的。

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.070
Not being understood by friends or family can also make you angry.
不被朋友或家人理解，也可能让你生气。

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:22.490
Although it’s OK to feel angry sometimes, it’s not healthy when anger takes over.
虽然有时生气没关系，但愤怒一旦占了上风，就不健康了。

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:27.280
You might act in a negative way and it can make you hurt others or yourself.
你可能会做出不好的举动，这可能会让你伤害别人或自己。

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.710
Next time you feel angry, try these simple ways to calm down.
下次生气时，试试用这些简单的方法让自己平静下来。

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:33.840
You can take a deep breath.
你可以深呼吸一下。

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.060
Deep breathing helps your body get away from the “angry energy”.
深呼吸能帮助你的身体摆脱“愤怒的能量”。

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.720
Taking some time to relax is also a good choice.
花些时间放松也是个不错的选择。

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.930
For example, you can take a short walk, listen to soft music or do simple exercise.
例如，你可以散一会儿步、听听轻柔的音乐，或者做些简单的运动。

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.720
Share your feelings with someone you trust.
和你信任的人分享你的感受。

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.070
It gives you a break from feeling unhappy all alone.
这能让你暂时不再独自一人闷闷不乐。

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.990
When you talk to them about your anger, they might help you see things in a calmer way.
你和对方谈起自己的愤怒时，对方也许能帮你更平静地看待事情。
